# URL hosts allowed inside the shipped app (QA-R60, PLT-R906). Adding a host needs a decision record
# and a /rieng-tu update in the same PR. One host per line; "*.example.org" allows subdomains.
#
# Not listed here because scripts/check-url-hosts.sh derives them from scripts/brand.env:
#   - the site and appcast host (APP_SITE_HOST);
#   - the repository host for issue forms opened by "Open GitHub issue" (PLT-R1205): the host of
#     APP_REPOSITORY_URL, github.com while that value is empty;
#   - the support mail domain (QA-R51): the domain of APP_SUPPORT_EMAIL when set.

# GitHub release asset hosts, only relevant if Pa chooses GitHub Releases for archives (PLT-R906,
# spec/02-platform.md section 14 item 4). Keep while that option exists in scripts/publish-release.
objects.githubusercontent.com
release-assets.githubusercontent.com

# Identifiers that are never contacted: XML namespaces and DTD URIs inside property lists and the
# Sparkle framework's appcast parser. VERIFY this list against the first real Release build.
www.apple.com
apple.com
www.w3.org
www.andymatuschak.org
sparkle-project.org
purl.org
ns.adobe.com

# Attribution text that is never contacted: source URLs quoted in Sparkle's licence, which About & Support shows
# verbatim (ShellCore/Settings/SparkleNotice.swift, ENG-R811-style acknowledgement of bsdiff and sais-lite).
www.daemonology.net
sites.google.com
